 "text": "Hello, how are you today? depends on your riding style. Generally, after 50 to 60 kilometers, or about 30 to 40 miles, it's a good idea to give them a good inflate. It' not just about the pressure. You should feel it in your hands. It not too firm, not too mushy. It' just the right pressure. Yeah, that's a good first step. The next step is to feel it. You can use a gauge of some kind. A floor pump will give you a better reading, but even a small hand pump will give you a pretty good idea. Yeah, that's a good point. Rain can really wear down the rubber. You definitely go lower, like a few psi. But I'd still inflate them a bit more than usual after rain.",
